      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should argue that the old curators are perpetuating a colonial mindset by treating objects as static commodities to be hoarded for Western consumption rather than living cultural assets belonging to their source communities. True preservation is not about keeping artifacts locked away in glass cases for \"future generations\" to study, but about ensuring these items are cared for by the communities that created them, which is the only way to guarantee their long-term survival and authenticity. By framing centralized collection as a form of cultural theft that actively harms the source communities, you can demonstrate that dismantling this system is not destroying history, but rather saving it from the very institutions that have historically exploited it.",
      "source": "target",
